From: kbuild <kbuild@localhost>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 20:55:05 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] genksyms: keep capability-gated __counted_by out of the GKI symbol CRCs

Folding a compiler-capability-gated attribute into a type makes the CRCs that
genksyms computes for the GKI ABI drift away from the Android GKI reference
values.  Prebuilt vendor modules then refuse to load ("disagrees about version
of symbol ..." / "Unknown symbol ..."); with qcom-scm.ko on icc_set_bw this
took down Q6/ADSP and hung the boot on any clang >= 19.1.3, which enables
CONFIG_CC_HAS_COUNTED_BY.

Expand such attributes to nothing under __GENKSYMS__, while leaving them intact
for the real compiler.  The only such attribute in this tree is __counted_by.

---
 include/linux/compiler_types.h | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/linux/compiler_types.h b/include/linux/compiler_types.h
index ed1c10712..2548b0fcf 100644
--- a/include/linux/compiler_types.h
+++ b/include/linux/compiler_types.h
@@ -320,8 +320,24 @@ struct ftrace_likely_data {
  * __bdos on clang < 19.1.3 can be off by 4:
  * https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/112636
  */
+/*
+ * Compiler-capability-gated attributes must never reach the symbol CRCs that
+ * genksyms computes for the GKI ABI.  Those CRCs are fixed by the Android GKI
+ * reference build; folding a capability-conditional attribute into a type makes
+ * our CRCs drift, and prebuilt vendor modules then refuse to load with
+ * "disagrees about version of symbol ..." / "Unknown symbol ..." (observed with
+ * qcom-scm.ko on icc_set_bw, which took down Q6/ADSP and hung the boot).
+ *
+ * Under __GENKSYMS__ such attributes are therefore expanded to nothing, while
+ * the real compiler still receives them.  Add any future capability-gated type
+ * attribute to this same #ifdef __GENKSYMS__ guard.
+ */
 #ifdef CONFIG_CC_HAS_COUNTED_BY
+# ifdef __GENKSYMS__
+#  define __counted_by(member)
+# else
 # define __counted_by(member)		__attribute__((__counted_by__(member)))
+# endif
 #else
 # define __counted_by(member)
 #endif
